WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.622
Code can be replaced a piece at
a time, but data moves once,

2
00:00:03.622 --> 00:00:07.350
and the move isn't done until
you can prove nothing was lost.

3
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:11.433
So the program treats it as
three jobs: convert the schema,

4
00:00:11.433 --> 00:00:15.950
move the rows, and prove the result,
looping back on any mismatch.

5
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:19.512
Choosing the engine is usually
settled by what you already run.

6
00:00:19.512 --> 00:00:23.687
And remember that the engine also decides
which conversion tools you can use.

7
00:00:23.687 --> 00:00:29.613
If the target is SQL Server, arrive
already on Book 6's modern sign-in pattern.

8
00:00:29.613 --> 00:00:31.920
Next, where conversions go wrong.
